Scenario: You are working in a modern Spring Boot environment (where circular references are strictly banned by default). A developer creates a @Configuration class and writes a @PostConstruct method that programmatically calls a local @Bean method inside the exact same class. The application crashes on startup with a BeanCurrentlyInCreationException.
